    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2RmSCthVhDJigEz8aUhxL9B)_\n\n## What\n\n- New module `sp-backup-lookup` (doc `docs/tangles/funct/sp-backup-lookup.org`, tests tangled from it).\n- `sp-backup-lookup-list FILE`: finds the backups of a file in every module's backup folder, newest first.\n- `M-x sp-backup-open`: pick a backup of the current file and open it read-only.\n- `M-x sp-backup-diff`: diff a backup against the file (prefix: Ediff).\n- In batch reports: `b` opens and `D` diffs a backup of the file linked on the line at point.\n\n## Why one lookup\n\n- Each module keeps its own backup folder and layout (`STAMP/name`, `name.STAMP`, `STAMP/full/path`, `STAMP/files/...`).\n- Modules are unchanged; the lookup reads all of them through `sp-backup-lookup-directories` (BibTeX lint, litnote titles/meta/refs, meta order, footnote lint, author notes, notes filing).\n- Backups with only a name (`STAMP/name`) cannot be told apart by folder, so same-named notes are all listed.\n\n## Tested\n\n- 7 ERT tests on fake backup folders in each layout (Emacs 29.3), plus the existing batch-report tests.\n- Not run: Sia's real backup folders and vault, GUI.\n- No CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi91pgzShS4iVhxjV5L)_",
